Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Imagine the ground under your feet\Nstopping for exactly one second.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.32,0:00:09.52,Default,,0,0,0,,At the equator, you are already moving east\Nat about 465 meters per second.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.24,0:00:12.80,Default,,0,0,0,,The road stops, but your body keeps going.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.44,0:00:18.32,Default,,0,0,0,,In that single second, you move nearly 465 meters\Nrelative to the ground,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.32,0:00:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,about four football fields, without taking a step.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.84,0:00:25.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Gravity still holds you down. The danger is sideways.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.36,0:00:28.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The air, clouds, and ocean keep their momentum too.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.40,0:00:33.20,Default,,0,0,0,,When the ground starts again, land, air, water,\Nand everything loose are no longer aligned.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.76,0:00:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,That mismatch is the real disaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.32,0:00:39.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What moves first? You, the atmosphere, or the ocean?
